<article class="env-definition" id="02KA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02KA">Definition <span data-tag="02KA">29.49.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. We say $f$ is <em>finite locally free</em> if $f$ is affine and $f_*\mathcal{O}_ X$ is a finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module. In this case we say $f$ is has <em>rank</em> or <em>degree</em> $d$ if the sheaf $f_*\mathcal{O}_ X$ is finite locally free of degree $d$. </p>
</article>